.github/workflows/nodejs.yml
```name=.github/workflows/nodejs.yml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main, feature/initial-setup ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Use Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '18'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run test
```

How you can add these locally (commands)
- Clone / fetch and switch to the branch:
  - git clone git@github.com:Gharkan86/atharsocial.git
  - cd atharsocial
  - git fetch origin
  - git checkout feature/initial-setup
    - (if the branch doesn't exist locally: git checkout -b feature/initial-setup origin/feature/initial-setup)
- Create the files above in their paths, then:
  - git add .
  - git commit -m "Add scaffold: server, .gitignore, LICENSE, CONTRIBUTING, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, CI"
  - git push origin feature/initial-setup

Notes
- The CI uses npm ci which requires a package-lock.json. Locally you can run npm install to generate package-lock.json before pushing, or run npm install --package-lock-only.
- After you push, I can open a pull request from feature/initial-setup into main, add further scaffolding (frontend or other), or add tests/linters.

What would you like me to do next?
- I can retry pushing the files to feature/initial-setup if you update the repository permissions for me.
- Or I can continue from here and prepare additional files (frontend scaffold, README updates, GitHub templates) and present them for you to add.
